id: pm-slack-rjb1
title: Disambiguate outbox receipt identities when historical state hashes repeat
description: "SDK history state hashes can repeat at different mutation versions. Existing delivery receipt keys use item, event and state hash, so an imported or replayed repeated state can share a receipt with another occurrence. Offline explanations now accept the SDK event version and explicitly withhold receipt attribution when a state hash repeats; migrating durable receipt identity is separate mutating-state work."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: follow-up,outbox
created_at: "2026-10-26T00:50:17.457Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T00:51:27.279Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Bind new delivery idempotency keys to the SDK mutation version and expected target revision, preserve and qualify legacy receipts, and verify old-input replay and concurrent recovery/draining with real no-git SDK trackers."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T00:51:27.279Z",codex-agent,Discovered while implementing pm-slack-slyv. Read-only explanations conservatively handle repeated state hashes; this item tracks the separate durable-key migration and replay/concurrency verification.
body: ""
